;; clj-kondo does not know that test.check's `defspec` defines a var, so every
;; property test read as an unresolved symbol -- 8 of this project's 9 findings
;; were that one gap. Teaching the linter is the fix; suppressing the rule
;; would have hidden real unresolved symbols too.
{:lint-as {clojure.test.check.clojure-test/defspec clojure.core/def}}
